  "content": {
    "id": "v2-abdd48cbb-practice-slot-8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "For what values of $k$ would the graph of $x^2-8x+y^2+2y-k=0$ not exist?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k<-17$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-8x+16+y^2+2y+1&=k+17\\\\(x-4)^2+(y+1)^2&=k+17\\end{align*}$$\nThe left-hand side is non-negative, so there are no real points when\n$$\\begin{align*}k+17&<0\\\\k&<-17\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
